<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese money supply rose 8.7 pct yr/yr in Feb.</title>
<headline>Portuguese money supply rose 8.7 pct yr/yr in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese money supply, as measured by &quot;aggregate 'L&quot;, roughly equivalent to M3, rose 8.7 percent year-on-year in February, compared with 9.3 percent in January, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>Domestic bank lending grew 13.8 percent year-on-year, compared with 11.7 percent the previous month.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
